<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Villain Arc — the app bundle's privacy manifest.

  Two separate claims live here, and they are separate on purpose:

  * What the FCT ACCOUNT holds. Everything the app authors syncs to the FCT platform under the
    user's account (Documentation/SYNC_FLOW.md names the 25 tables), so it is account-scoped and
    therefore LINKED to identity. It exists to serve the user their own data on their own devices:
    app functionality, never analytics and never tracking. Apple Health data is read on-device and
    re-derived per device — it never rides the wire — but the goals the user sets over it do.

  * What DIAGNOSTICS hold. Crash and performance payloads, the breadcrumb trail, funnels and
    feature counters. These key on a locally-minted install id and carry no account token, so
    there is no path — schema, wire, or key — that joins them to an account: NOT linked to
    identity, and structurally so rather than by promise.

  Nothing here tracks, so NSPrivacyTracking is false and there are no tracking domains.

  Every required-reason entry below names code this bundle actually runs:
  * UserDefaults — the App Group suite shared with the widget and intents extension
    (SharedModelContainer.sharedDefaults), plus FCTAccount's own standard-domain session state.
  * File timestamps — FCTMetrics reads the modification date of the diagnostic payload files it
    wrote inside this app's own container.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeName</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
